<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111724" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλεγμ-αίνω</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφλέγμηνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					276
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				64.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				4.49
			</span></i>; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ᾱνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Na.</u>
					3.19
				</span></i>
			: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> trans.,
				<i>causeto swell up</i>; of food, <i>fill, nourish,</i> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσχναίνω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Loc.Hom.</u>
				34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			 intr., <i>to be heated, inflamed, fester,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				5.58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prog.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i> l. c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πληγὴφλεγμαίνουσα</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Is.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>, cf.Ar.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				85b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>to be swollen,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Loc.Hom.</u>
				13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the sea,
				<i>seethe,</i> M.Ant.l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦμα φλεγμαῖνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					5.17
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλεγμαίνουσα πόλις,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑγιής,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				372e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχὴ φλεγμαίνουσα,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπαργῶσα καὶ θυμουμένη</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				691e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ φ. τῶν πραγμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			; of feelings, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.86.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				7.21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ στρατιῶται ἐφλέγμηναν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
				</span></i>
			 l. c.; also of luxury, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυτελεῖς καὶ φλεγμαίνουσαι τράπεζαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.66o
				</span></i>
			f; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐν Βαβυλῶνι
				φλεγμαίνοντα,</span> of <i>extravagant</i> court
			ceremonial, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				2.25
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
